{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirShape","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirShape","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionOfComposition"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirShape.garnirShape_lexGt_example","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirShape.garnirShape_lexGt_example","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GarnirShape.lean#L142-L143","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirShape.garnirShape_lexGt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirShape.garnirShape_lexGt","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GarnirShape.lean#L120-L127","doc":"**Mathas' Lemma 3.12, shape half.**  The Garnir shape is lex-greater than `μ`.\n\nThe witness is `μ.colLen (μ.rowLen i)` — the number of rows longer than row `i` —\nwhich is the `c = #{r : λ_r > λᵢ}` measured 1435/1435 by the probe, and is **not**\nthe Garnir row `i`: at `λ = (2,2,2)` with node `(1,0)` the shape moves at row `0`,\nbecause the merged part overtakes the rows above `i` that tie with `λᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirShape.colLen_garnirShape_at","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirShape.colLen_garnirShape_at","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GarnirShape.lean#L102-L118","doc":"At the threshold `λᵢ` the Garnir shape has exactly one more part above it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirShape.colLen_garnirShape_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirShape.colLen_garnirShape_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GarnirShape.lean#L79-L100","doc":"The two column-length facts `lexGt_of_colLen` wants, at the threshold `λᵢ`.\n\nAbove `λᵢ` nothing changes: the three new parts are `j ≤ λᵢ₊₁ − 1 ≤ λᵢ`,\n`λᵢ + 1`, and `λᵢ₊₁ − j − 1 ≤ λᵢ`, and the two they replace are `λᵢ` and `λᵢ₊₁` —\nso for a threshold `m > λᵢ` every one of the five is at most `m`, except `λᵢ + 1`,\nwhich is at most `m` too.  At `m = λᵢ` exactly one of the five clears the bar, and\nit is `λᵢ + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirShape.countP_garnirComp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirShape.countP_garnirComp","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GarnirShape.lean#L69-L77","doc":"The count of `garnirComp` splits into the shared outer part and the three new\nentries; the shared part is the same one `μ.rowLens` contributes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirShape.succ_lt_length_rowLens","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirShape.succ_lt_length_rowLens","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GarnirShape.lean#L64-L67","doc":"A Garnir node makes row `i+1` non-empty, so both rows are inside `rowLens`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirShape.garnirShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirShape.garnirShape","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GarnirShape.lean#L60-L62","doc":"**The Garnir shape**: the partition of that composition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirShape.garnirComp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirShape.garnirComp","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GarnirShape.lean#L55-L58","doc":"**Mathas' Garnir composition**, as a list of parts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirShape.countP_split_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirShape.countP_split_two","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GarnirShape.lean#L38-L51","doc":"Splitting a list's count at two consecutive positions.\n\n`countP` is additive over `++`, and `drop` peels one entry at a time, so a list's\ncount is its count outside a two-entry window plus the two entries' own\ncontributions.  Both the original shape and the Garnir composition are read this\nway, and they share the two outer summands verbatim. ","signatureChunk":0}]}